{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/out-layer/outlayer/pulls/29","id":4175142488,"node_id":"PR_kwDOP_e_4c74255Y","html_url":"https://github.com/out-layer/outlayer/pull/29","diff_url":"https://github.com/out-layer/outlayer/pull/29.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/out-layer/outlayer/pull/29.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/out-layer/outlayer/issues/29","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/out-layer/outlayer/pulls/29/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/out-layer/outlayer/pulls/29/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/out-layer/outlayer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/out-layer/outlayer/issues/29/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/out-layer/outlayer/statuses/9fc3569807869339a34865543c42bcc463b27be6","number":29,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add MCP server exposing OutLayer docs for AI coding assistants","user":{"login":"ayushsingh82","id":121667116,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0B-LA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121667116?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82","html_url":"https://github.com/ayushsingh82","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayushsingh82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nThere's currently no MCP server for OutLayer — devs using an AI coding assistant (Claude Code, Claude Desktop, etc.) to integrate with OutLayer have no structured way to get accurate docs into the assistant's context, short of manually pasting files in. I went looking for one (checked `docs/`, dashboard docs, and grepped the whole repo for `mcp`/`model context protocol`) and came up empty, so this fills that gap.\n\n- Adds `mcp-server/`, a small stdio [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server built on `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`.\n- Exposes ~55 developer-facing docs from across the repo (root docs, `docs/`, and component READMEs — contract, worker, keystore-worker, keystore-dao-contract, register-contract, vault-contract, dashboard, wasi-examples, etc.) as MCP **resources**, addressable as `outlayer-docs://<path>`.\n- Deliberately excludes internal/non-technical files: `CLAUDE.md` (AI-assistant working instructions), `Onepager.md`, `ORACLE_RFP_PROPOSAL.md`, `RFP_RESPONSE.md`, `CHANGELOG_GITHUB_COMPILATION.md`.\n- Docs-only for v1 — no live API calls. Wiring the HTTPS API in as MCP **tools** (using the existing OpenAPI spec) is a natural follow-up, noted in the README.\n- `package-lock.json` is committed (mirrors the existing exception for `dashboard/package-lock.json` in `.gitignore` — this is a tool devs `npm install` and run directly, not a library, so the build should be reproducible).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm install` / `npm run build` succeed cleanly in `mcp-server/`\n- [x] Verified every path in `src/docs.ts` resolves to an existing file (57/57)\n- [x] Smoke-tested the server over stdio: `initialize` → `resources/list` → `resources/read` for `outlayer-docs://README.md` all return correct MCP responses\n- [ ] Manual test in Claude Desktop / Claude Code MCP config (left for reviewer, since it depends on local client setup)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-31T04:55:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T07:31:04Z","closed_at":"2026-07-31T07:26:15Z","merged